{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceTLUniqueness","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.RowCapObstruction"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weightAlt_ne_zero_at_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weightAlt_ne_zero_at_three","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L353-L362","doc":"**`hN : N = 2` is load-bearing: the premise alone does not give\nTemperley–Lieb.**\n\nAt `N = 3` the class admits an instance whose alternating weight is nonzero, so\n`weightAlt_eq_zero_at_two` really consumes the two-dimensionality of the fibre\n— i.e. `thm:su2-emergence` is used, not decorative. Equivalently: were the mass\nfibre three-dimensional, the fibre-categorical premise would be compatible with\na nonzero `(1³)` weight, hence with convention C. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exists_fibre_categorical_markov_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exists_fibre_categorical_markov_trace","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L323-L351","doc":"**The premise is satisfiable at `dim V = 2`, and convention D realises it.**\n\nThere exists a trace satisfying the fibre-categorical premise at `N = 2`\n*together with* all three Markov equations — namely the Jones weight vector\n`(1 − 2t², t², 0)` at Ocneanu parameter `z = q − t`, `t = [2]_q⁻¹`. Its\nparameter satisfies `z·[2]_q = q²`, exactly the conclusion of\n`markovWeights_eq_jones_of_fibre_categorical`.\n\nSo the conditional theorem is **not** vacuously true: its antecedent has a\nmodel, and the model is the convention production already uses. What remains\nopen is not whether such a trace exists but whether the *mass channel's* trace\nis one — bean `qou-n1dj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.fibreCategoricalJones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.fibreCategoricalJones","kind":"def","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L301-L321","doc":"Convention D as a model of the premise at `N = 2`: weights\n`(1 − 2t², t², 0)` with `t = [2]_q⁻¹`, i.e. `y_(2,1) = 1/[2]_q²` and\n`y_(1³) = 0` — the Jones / Temperley–Lieb closure.\n\nThe row-cap fields hold because at `N = 2` the alternating weight is `0` by\nconstruction while the symmetric and mixed channels are present\n(`weylDimSym 2 = 4`, `weylDimMixed 2 = 2`), and non-degeneracy holds because\n`[2]_q²·t² = 1` makes `t² ≠ 0` in any nontrivial ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.fibreCategoricalAtThree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.fibreCategoricalAtThree","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L278-L290","doc":"Witness instance at `N = 3`: all three Weyl dimensions are nonzero there\n(`10`, `8`, `1`), so every row-cap implication is vacuously satisfied and the\nalternating weight is free to be nonzero. Used only by\n`weightAlt_ne_zero_at_three` to show `hN : N = 2` is load-bearing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.fibre_ne_zero_of_zero_dimensional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.fibre_ne_zero_of_zero_dimensional","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L259-L276","doc":"**The premise plus normalisation forces a nonempty fibre.**\n\nAt `N = 0` every Weyl dimension vanishes (`C(2,3) = C(1,3) = C(0,3) = 0`), so\nall three row-cap fields fire and the trace is identically zero — contradicting\n`tr 1 = 1`. Hence the row-cap fields have genuine content: they are strong\nenough to be *refutable* against normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ocneanu_eq_jones_of_fibre_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ocneanu_eq_jones_of_fibre_categorical","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L231-L252","doc":"**Convention C is excluded under the premise.**\n\nContrapositive of the conditional theorem in the form that separates the two\nproduction conventions: a mass-channel trace satisfying the fibre-categorical\npremise at `dim V = 2` **cannot** have an Ocneanu parameter with\n`z·[2]_q ≠ q²`. Applied to the Wenzl `z`-trace at\n`z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})` (convention C), this says C is not the categorical\ntrace of a two-dimensional fibre action on `V^{⊗3}`.\n\nAgain conditional: it excludes C *given* the premise, not absolutely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovWeights_eq_jones_of_fibre_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovWeights_eq_jones_of_fibre_categorical","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L186-L229","doc":"**Conditional theorem — the fibre-categorical premise plus `dim V = 2`\nforces convention D.**\n\nLet the mass-channel trace satisfy the premise `MassTraceIsFibreCategorical`\n(the categorical trace of the fibre action on `V^{⊗3}`; the one open input),\nlet the fibre be two-dimensional (`hN : N = 2`, supplied by\n`thm:su2-emergence`), and let the three Markov equations hold against the\n`H₃(q)` `q`-character table on the class representatives `1`, `σ₀`, `σ₀σ₁`,\n\n  `tr 1 = 1`,   `tr σ₀ = z`,   `tr σ₀σ₁ = z²`\n\n(hypotheses `hnorm`, `hsigma`, `hsigmasigma`; `qi` is `q⁻¹`, constrained by\n`hqi : q * qi = 1`, so the statement is division-free).\n\nThen the weight vector and the Ocneanu parameter are completely determined:\n\n  `[2]_q² · y_(2,1) = 1`,   `y_(3) = 1 − 2 y_(2,1)`,   `z · [2]_q = q²`,\n\nwith `[2]_q = q + qi`. Solving the first gives `y = ([4]_q/[2]_q³, 1/[2]_q², 0)`\n— the Jones / Temperley–Lieb closure, **convention D**. Convention C, whose\nOcneanu parameter satisfies `z·[2]_q ≠ q²`, is thereby excluded.\n\n**This is an implication, not a resolution.** The conclusion is derived — from\nthe class fields (which mention neither `q` nor `z` nor D), the proved row-cap\nobstruction, and the proved Markov-trace uniqueness theorem. What it buys is\nthat the D-vs-C question now rests on exactly one named, unproved premise\ninstead of on a numerical coincidence with CODATA. Whether the mass channel\nsatisfies that premise is bean `qou-n1dj`, and it is open. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:markov-trace-frobenius-selection","label":"prop:markov-trace-frobenius-selection","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-frobenius-selection.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightMixed_ne_zero_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightMixed_ne_zero_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L175-L182","doc":"**Faithfulness on `TL₃`, derived from the premise at `dim V = 2`.**\n\nAt `N = 2` the mixed channel *is* present (`weylDimMixed 2 = 2`, the spin-`1/2`\ndoublet), so the non-degeneracy field forces its weight to be nonzero. This is\nthe link that excludes the degenerate root `z = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightAlt_eq_zero_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightAlt_eq_zero_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L165-L173","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb condition, derived from the premise at `dim V = 2`.**\n\nAt `N = 2` the alternating Schur–Weyl channel is absent\n(`weylDimAlt 2 = C(2,3) = 0`, `weyl_dim_alt_eq_zero_iff`), so the row-cap field\nof the premise forces its Frobenius weight to vanish. This is the link that\nturns `thm:su2-emergence` into the Temperley–Lieb condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightMixed_ne_zero_of_dim_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightMixed_ne_zero_of_dim_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L161-L161","doc":"Non-degeneracy: a mixed channel the fibre supplies is genuinely carried.\nEquivalently, faithfulness on `TL₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightAlt_eq_zero_of_dim_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightAlt_eq_zero_of_dim_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L158-L158","doc":"Row-cap support in the alternating channel — the field that, at `N = 2`,\nsupplies the Temperley–Lieb condition `y_(1³) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightMixed_eq_zero_of_dim_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightMixed_eq_zero_of_dim_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L155-L155","doc":"Row-cap support in the mixed channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightSym_eq_zero_of_dim_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightSym_eq_zero_of_dim_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L153-L153","doc":"Row-cap support in the symmetric channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightAlt","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L151-L151","doc":"Frobenius weight of the alternating channel `λ = (1³)`; this is the block\nthe row cap kills at `N = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightMixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightMixed","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L148-L148","doc":"Frobenius weight of the mixed channel `λ = (2,1)`; this is the\nTemperley–Lieb / two-row block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.weightSym","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L145-L145","doc":"Frobenius weight of the symmetric channel `λ = (3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical.mk","kind":"ctor","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MassTraceIsFibreCategorical","kind":"class","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones.lean#L112-L161","doc":"**The one open premise, axiomatised: the mass-channel trace is the\ncategorical trace of the fibre action on `V^{⊗3}`.**\n\nAn instance records the three Frobenius weights `(y_(3), y_(2,1), y_(1³))` of\nthe mass-channel trace on `H₃(q)`, together with the two support properties\nthat follow from its being the categorical trace of the action of a fibre of\ndimension `N`:\n\n* `weight*_eq_zero_of_dim_eq_zero` — **row-cap support.** Quantum Schur–Weyl\n  duality decomposes `V^{⊗3} = ⊕_{λ ⊢ 3} S^λ ⊗ V_λ` with the row cap\n  `ℓ(λ) ≤ N`; a partition violating the cap has `dim V_λ = 0` and therefore\n  contributes no summand at all. A trace computed *from the fibre action* can\n  put no weight on a channel that is absent from the module it acts on.\n\n* `weightMixed_ne_zero_of_dim_ne_zero` — **non-degeneracy / faithfulness.**\n  Conversely a channel the fibre genuinely supplies is genuinely seen: its\n  weight is nonzero. This is faithfulness on the surviving (Temperley–Lieb)\n  part, and it is what excludes the degenerate root `z = q` of the\n  Temperley–Lieb condition (`markovWeights_degenerate_root`).\n\nBoth properties are independent of the deformation parameter, because the row\ncap constrains `dim V` and quantisation does not change dimensions.\n\n**What is not asserted.** The weight *magnitudes*. At `q ≠ 1` these are quantum\ndimensions rather than the classical Weyl dimensions `weylDim*`, so pinning\nthem to the classical values would be false. Nothing here mentions `q`, the\nOcneanu parameter, or the Jones weight vector — those appear only in the\n*conclusions* of the theorems below.\n\nAn instance of this class is not a proof of the premise; it is the premise,\nnamed. Bean `qou-n1dj` is open on whether the mass channel admits one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}